@meta
	company: ACME Corp
	amount: $1,000,000
@end

# Table Corpus Tests

This file exercises all table LDOC features.

## Basic Table

Simple table with header row (first row) and data rows:

@table
	[Header 1, Header 2, Header 3]
	[Cell A1, Cell A2, Cell A3]
	[Cell B1, Cell B2, Cell B3]
	[Cell C1, Cell C2, Cell C3]

## Horizontal Merge (Colspan)

Use `>` in a cell to merge with the cell to its left:

@table
	[Column A, Column B, Column C]
	[Spans two columns, >, Normal cell]
	[Normal, Spans two columns, >]
	[All three columns span, >, >]
	[A, B, C]

## Vertical Merge (Rowspan)

Use `^` in a cell to merge with the cell above it:

@table
	[Header A, Header B, Header C]
	[Spans down, Value 1, Value 2]
	[^, Value 3, Value 4]
	[^, Value 5, Value 6]
	[Normal, Normal, Normal]

## Combined Horizontal and Vertical Merge

Both colspan and rowspan in the same table:

@table
	[A, B, C, D]
	[Spans 2x2, >, Normal C, Normal D]
	[^, >, More C, More D]
	[Bottom A, Bottom B, Bottom C, Bottom D]

@table
	[Col 1, Col 2, Col 3]
	[Wide cell, >, Tall cell]
	[Regular 1, Regular 2, ^]
	[Regular 3, Regular 4, ^]

## Inline Formatting in Cells

Cells can contain **bold**, *italic*, and other inline formatting:

@table
	[**Bold Header**, *Italic Header*, Normal Header]
	[**bold text**, *italic text*, normal text]
	[mixed **bold** and *italic*, plain, more plain]
	[`inline code`, plain, more plain]

## Variables in Cells

Cells can contain variable references (defined at top of file):

@table
	[Field, Value]
	[Company Name, {{company}}]
	[Contract Amount, {{amount}}]
	[Description, Payment to {{company}} for {{amount}}]

## Quoting Cell Values

Special characters and merge markers can be quoted:

@table
	[Header, Special Values]
	[Comma in cell, "Hello, World"]
	[Greater than literal, ">"]
	[Caret literal, "^"]
	[Leading space, " starts with space"]
	[Trailing space, "ends with space "]
	[Quote marks, "He said ""hello"""]

## Single Column Table

@table
	[Single Column Header]
	[Row 1]
	[Row 2]
	[Row 3]

## Single Row Table (Header Only)

@table
	[Column A, Column B, Column C]

## Empty Cells

@table
	[Header A, Header B, Header C]
	[, Value 2, Value 3]
	[Value 1, , Value 3]
	[Value 1, Value 2, ]
	[, , ]

## Complex Merge Pattern

@table
	[A, B, C, D, E]
	[Span 3 cols, >, >, D1, E1]
	[A2, B2, C2, Span 2 rows, E2]
	[A3, B3, C3, ^, E3]
	[Span 2x2, >, C4, D4, E4]
	[^, >, C5, D5, E5]

## Table with @end Marker

@table
	[With End, Header 2]
	[Row 1, Data 1]
	[Row 2, Data 2]
@end

Some text after the table.

## Multiple Tables in Sequence

First table:

@table
	[Table 1 Col A, Table 1 Col B]
	[T1 R1 A, T1 R1 B]

Second table:

@table
	[Table 2 Col A, Table 2 Col B]
	[T2 R1 A, T2 R1 B]

## Table with Links

@table
	[Link Type, Example]
	[Plain link, [Click here](https://example.com)]
	[Bold link, [**Bold link**](https://example.org)]

## Long Cell Content

@table
	[Short, Long Content Column]
	[A, This is a much longer piece of text that demonstrates how cells handle longer content strings]
	[B, Another long cell with plenty of words to fill the space]

End of table corpus tests.
